			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T08:33:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Gate asset deployment strategy behind $TierSchemeAssets env var\n\nAdvance the Mountain submodule with a build-time gating mechanism that selects between two asset deployment modes: Embedded (default, assets Brotli-compressed into the binary) and FileSystem (full disk layout in Contents/Resources/ served via the localhost plugin static_root fallback).\n\nbuild.rs reads $TierSchemeAssets (defaults to \"Embedded\") and mutates tauri.conf.json at build time accordingly — Embedded sets frontendDist=\"../Sky/Target\" with minimal bundle.resources (bootstrap, extensions, nls, node_modules, product.json), while FileSystem sets frontendDist=null and maps the full Sky/Target tree. LocalhostPlugin.rs wraps the static_root disk-fallback code in #[cfg(feature = \"TierSchemeAssetsFileSystem\")] so it compiles only when FileSystem mode is active. The feature flag is added to IsDeclaredTierFeature rather than being a silent default.\n\nThis completes the foundation laid by the Static/Application/ prefix refactoring, making the deployment mode selectable at build time via a single environment variable rather than manual tauri.conf.json editing.",
			"SHA": "0211d129196ffef2b812a8e3c1ab1d58211d703b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T08:22:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Advance 5 Element submodules with Mountain bundle consolidation and style normalisation across configs\n\nAdvance five Land/Element submodules in a coordinated update that restructures Mountain's Tauri bundle layout and normalises indentation conventions across the remaining four.\n\n**Mountain** consolidates bundle resources under a `Static/Application/` prefix, unifying the flat bundle layout (Contents/Resources/extensions) with the monorepo dev layout (Sky/Target/Static/Application/extensions) under a single source of truth. `tauri.conf.json` remaps all resource entries to `Static/Application/...`, sets `frontendDist` to null so the dev server delegates to the localhost plugin's disk fallback, and adds `static_root` resolution in LocalhostPlugin.rs that probes both production and dev paths. ScanPathConfigure.rs registers the new canonical extensions path before legacy flat paths, which are retained as fallback for existing development environments.\n\n**Cocoon, Output, Wind, and Worker** align their ESBuild configuration files and compiled artifacts to the project-wide tab-based indentation convention (reversing the 2-space style from a prior pass), with trailing commas, import-before-declaration ordering, and consolidated export blocks applied across all config modules. Output additionally hoists static imports above helper shim declarations for a consistent imports-first preamble order.\n\nZero functional changes across Cocoon, Output, Wind, and Worker — build outputs and runtime behaviour are identical. Mountain retains flat-path fallbacks so existing dev runs and CI pipelines continue unbroken during the migration.",
			"SHA": "9ea797675c2545ab8721abb6954fb4e70661ab16"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T06:38:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				5
			],
			"Message": "style(Project): Normalize indentation across 5 Element submodule configs\n\nAdvance five Land/Element submodules with formatting consistency passes across ESBuild configuration files, compiled output artifacts, and Tauri configuration.\n\n**Cocoon** converts all Configuration/ESBuild/*.js files from tab to 2-space indentation, reorders import/export declarations so re-exports appear before local imports, and deduplicates default import aliases in Target.js. RouteManifest timestamp updated and Target/ artifacts regenerated.\n\n**Mountain** reverts the verbose DevelopmentNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency naming scheme from a prior transitional debug phase, restoring the stable `\"fiddee.editor.binary\"` identifier and `\"Mountain\"` productName in tauri.conf.json, along with collapsing externalBin/targets arrays back to single-line format. Backup files created alongside the verbose identifiers are deleted.\n\n**Output** consolidates compiled JavaScript artifacts under Configuration/ to uniform 2-space indentation with hoisted helper shims, stripped trailing commas, and multi-line export blocks — semantically identical to their tab-indented predecessors.\n\n**Wind** reformats all ESBuild configuration modules under Configuration/ESBuild/ to 2-space indentation and reorders import/export to a declaration-before-export pattern.\n\n**Worker** applies 2-space indentation to Target.js and Worker.js ESBuild configs, collapses single-line arrow functions, and expands exports to multi-line named blocks.\n\nZero functional changes across all five submodules — build outputs and runtime behaviour are identical.",
			"SHA": "cf4b0c66a6b82012bbe224c00afeb69bbfedc1ec"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T06:14:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Extract Cocoon namespace maps, Mountain dispatchers\n\nAdvance three Element submodules with structural extractions, runtime fixes, and formatting alignment.\n\n**Cocoon** lifts the inline RegisterCustomEditor function and six shared registry maps (CustomEditorProviders, CustomEditorProvidersByViewType, TreeDataProviders, TreeDataProvidersByViewId, WebviewViewProviders, WebviewViewBuilders, WebviewPanels) from Namespace.ts into dedicated RegisterCustomEditor.ts and Registry.ts modules. Namespace.ts shrinks by ~170 lines and re-exports the relocated maps through the existing path, preserving all provider registration and lifecycle behaviour unchanged.\n\n**Mountain** extracts the 1400-line `process_mountain_request` and 600-line `send_mountain_notification` match blocks from CocoonService/mod.rs into GenericRequest::Dispatcher and GenericNotification::Dispatcher modules, reducing mod.rs by ~1900 lines and clarifying the gRPC service boundary. Three fixes accompany the refactor: (1) scope the MutexGuard on WorkspaceFolders to a block so it is dropped before any await point, restoring Send-ness for tauri::async_runtime::spawn; (2) replace the OnceLock that caches a permanent None (routing all dev logs to /tmp after the first failed resolution) with a two-phase RESOLVED/RETRY system that retries after Tauri creates the app-data directory; (3) replace a bare `return Ok(...)` inside a WindServiceHandlers match arm (which exited the enclosing async block and broke Scheduler::Submit's `Output = ()` bound) with an if/else expression. A clippy-nit removing redundant `.as_str()` in AliasPath.rs is included. Two follow-up style commits normalize dispatcher indentation and update Cargo.toml/tauri.conf.json build identifiers for the dev profile.\n\n**Worker** normalises indentation across all three ESBuild configuration files to hard tabs via two style-only commits (spaces → tabs, then tabs → fully aligned tabs). Zero functional changes — build output is identical.\n\nAll Target/ compiled artifacts and RouteManifest files are regenerated for Cocoon.",
			"SHA": "a74c89e53e1c6310ff031e05dafc682fd0b0c121"
		}
	],
